Subject: [PATCH 0003] Size the obmalloc radix tree by address bits
Upstream: CPython 3.13.7
Upstream-Archive: https://www.python.org/ftp/python/3.13.7/Python-3.13.7.tgz
Upstream-SHA256: 6c9d80839cfa20024f34d9a6dd31ae2a9cd97ff5e980e969209746037a5153b2
Build-Variants: capstone64 domain (musl)
Depends-On: cpython-3.13.7-0001-address-width.patch
Apply-From: upstream source root, with patch --batch --forward --fuzz=0 -p1

Include/internal/pycore_obmalloc.h sets POINTER_BITS, the number of address
bits the arena radix tree indexes, from SIZEOF_VOID_P and stops with #error
"obmalloc radix tree requires 64-bit or 32-bit pointers" otherwise. The tree
indexes addresses, so the width is the address width: 64 on capstone64. This
is the same decision the pymalloc component port made
(ports/cpython/pymalloc/patches/cpython-3.13.7-0002, "The radix tree indexes 64
address bits even when capabilities occupy 16 bytes").

The header's two other SIZEOF_VOID_P tests are left alone on purpose: ALIGNMENT
16 is the alignment a capability needs, and large pools and arenas are the
64-bit configuration the pymalloc port measured. Every core file includes this
header: 156 of the third survey's 206 failures.

--- a/Include/internal/pycore_obmalloc.h
+++ b/Include/internal/pycore_obmalloc.h
@@ -537,7 +537,7 @@
 
 */
 
-#if SIZEOF_VOID_P == 8
+#if _Py_SIZEOF_ADDRESS == 8
 
 /* number of bits in a pointer */
 #define POINTER_BITS 64
@@ -556,7 +556,7 @@
 /* use the top and mid layers of the radix tree */
 #define USE_INTERIOR_NODES
 
-#elif SIZEOF_VOID_P == 4
+#elif _Py_SIZEOF_ADDRESS == 4
 
 #define POINTER_BITS 32
 #define IGNORE_BITS 0
